diagnostic help: integer division must name its rounding. `div_trunc(a, b)` rounds toward zero and reproduces the previous result of `a / b`, but it may not be the rounding you need: `div_floor(a, b)` or `div_ceil(a, b)` is often intended. For a real quotient write `to_float(a) / to_float(b)`. While `a` is below `2 ^ 52` in magnitude, `to_int(round(to_float(a) / to_float(b)))` gives the nearest Int and `to_int(to_float(a) / to_float(b))` fails unless the division is exact; for larger values, binary64 rounding can break both guarantees
diagnostic code: graphcal::D043
